"யாணர்ப்","lemma":"யாணர்ப்","gloss":"fresh wealth"}],"gloss":"fresh wealth","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பயன்","parts":[{"text":"பயன்","lemma":"பயன்","gloss":"yield"}],"gloss":"yield"},{"surface":"திகழ்","parts":[{"text":"திகழ்","lemma":"திகழ்","gloss":"shine"}],"gloss":"shining"},{"surface":"வைப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"வைப்பு","lemma":"வைப்பு","gloss":"settlement"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"genitive suffix"}],"gloss":"of the settlements"},{"surface":"பிறர்","parts":[{"text":"பிறர்","lemma":"பிறர்","gloss":"others"}],"gloss":"of others"},{"surface":"அகன்றலை","parts":[{"text":"அகன்","lemma":"அகல்","gloss":"wide"},{"text":"தலை","lemma":"தலை","gloss":"place"}],"gloss":"wide area"},{"surface":"நாடே","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"நாடு","gloss":"country"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphatic particle"}],"gloss":"country indeed"}]}],"literal":"Legs that urged the male elephants / perfect feet that wore hero's anklets / with generous hands curved from fighting with arrows / with beautiful bow whose joints shine / with wide chest bearing scars / with strong power that moved the shield / not considering day and night, the enemies' / towns you burn, and with that light, amidst weeping cries and uproar / since you desire plunder, good things / become non-existent indeed, O Chola of the moving chariot! / The clamor of cool water spreading, blocking the soil / abounding like fish, with fresh wealth / where yield shines in settlements, the wide countries of others!","translation":"O Chola king of the swift chariot! Your legs have urged war elephants, your perfect feet wear hero's anklets, and your generous hands are curved from pulling arrows. Your beautiful bow has shining joints, your wide chest bears battle scars, and your great strength moves the shield. Without distinguishing between day and night, you desire to plunder your enemies. In the light of their burning towns, amidst weeping cries and loud uproar, all good things are lost. Those wide lands of others, once filled with the clamor of cool water spreading over the soil, abounding in fish and fresh wealth, and shining with rich settlements, are now laid to waste.","modern":"இயங்கும் தேரையுடைய சோழனே! களிறுகளைச் செலுத்திய கால்களையும், வீரக்கழல் அணிந்த திருந்திய அடிகளையும், அம்புகளை எய்து வளைந்த கொடைத் தன்மையுடைய கைகளையும், கணுக்கள் விளங்கும் அழகிய வில்லையும், வடுக்கள் நிறைந்த அகன்ற மார்பையும், கேடயத்தை ஏந்திய வலிமையையும் உடையவன் நீ. பகலையும் இரவையும் பாராமல், பகைவர்களுடைய ஊர்களைச் சுட்டெரிக்கும் நெருப்பின் வெளிச்சத்தில், அழுகைக் குரல்களும் ஆரவாரமும் ஒலிக்க, நீ கொள்ளையிடுவதையே விரும்புவதால், பிறருடைய அகன்ற நாடுகள் பாழாகின்றன. குளிர்ந்த நீர் பரவிப் பாயும் ஒலியும், மீன்கள் செறிந்து விளங்கும் புதுவருவாயும், பயன்கள் நிறைந்த ஊர்களும் கொண்ட அந்த வளமான நாடுகள், இப்போது நல்லவை யாவும் இல்லாதனவாக ஆகிவிட்டன.","explanation":"The poet Karuṅkuḻal Ātaṉār addresses the Chola king Karikāṟ Peruvaḷattāṉ in this poem belonging to the Vañci tiṇai. He praises the king's physical prowess, describing his battle-scarred chest, his legs that guide war elephants, and his hands curved from pulling bowstrings. The poet then details the relentless nature of the king's warfare, as he attacks his enemies day and night without rest. The central theme of Koṟṟavaḷḷai is highlighted by contrasting the current destruction of the enemy's land with its former prosperity. The lands that once thrived with abundant water, fish, and agricultural wealth are now reduced to ashes, illuminated only by the flames of burning towns and filled with the cries of the defeated.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}